  "rationale": {
    "Immersive": "Loot is no longer ubiquitous, free food HP is disabled, sleep heals partially, ammunition/medical restocking and resale remain useful but limited.",
    "Tactical": "Combat-readiness trades reduced ammunition pickups and treatment for lethal firefights, not inflated target health.",
    "Field Medic": "Medicine is more effective but costly and not limitless; medical crates receive a relative role exception, not general abundance.",
    "Mutant Hunter": "Wildlife/trophy rewards support expeditions, but ammo and treatment remain finite and encounter costs matter.",
    "Anomaly Runner": "Exploration and artifacts fund preparation; reduced general supplies and costly radiation treatment preserve exposure risk.",
    "Wanderer": "Sustained roaming keeps useful stamina/carry perks but makes food, medical supplies and fast travel meaningful expenses.",
    "Mercenary": "Contracts provide an income niche; ammunition and weapon upkeep consume much of the payout.",
    "Smuggler": "Better artifact/trophy margins do not negate sparse expedition supplies, repair costs and costly travel.",
    "Scavenger": "Salvage is useful but low-quality; fewer world supplies, weak medicine, repair expense and modest payout create genuine tradeoffs.",
    "Outcast": "Shelter and treatment are scarce; slightly moderated excessive wear/expenses avoid an unwinnable scarcity loop.",
    "Hardcore": "Risk, constrained supplies and preparation dominate, while slightly lower cumulative gear penalties and viable quest pay prevent pointless grind.",
    "Hardcore+": "Severe scarcity with finite but not zero recovery and income; toned-down damage/wear stacking keeps survival possible."
  },
